{
  "abstract": "Dujella, Kazalicki and Petričević constructed a two-parameter family of rational Diophantine sextuples; on Paper 10's chart (u, t1) it is the double cover z² = Q6 of P¹×P¹ given by one remaining square. Paper 10 showed that the two coordinate rulings of the locus of the almost septuple #4 on this surface have fibres of genus at least 5, and left open whether the locus contains other curves of genus at most one. We determine Kodaira dimensions. For each of the ten regular fifth elements g of the 4-subsets of the DKP quintuple, we compute the square-free part Q_g of the remaining condition. Two are identically zero, one is DKP's sixth element, and for each of the other seven every component of the septuple locus that dominates the plane is of general type, as is the almost-septuple locus of #4. The DKP sextuple surface itself, and the #4 seventh condition alone, are properly elliptic with χ = 4. The method is Horikawa's canonical resolution of double covers, exact over Q: singular points in all four charts by resultants, rational points resolved by successive blow-ups, and irrational orbits proved to be quadruple points with tangent cones free of triple roots. It is checked by an independent adjoint count of the geometric genus, by the minimal discriminant (degree 48) of the elliptic fibration, and by reproducing the Kodaira dimension one of Paper 50's surface. Non-density of rational points follows only under the Bombieri–Lang conjecture; seventh elements that are not regular fifths of 4-subsets of the quintuple are not treated.",
